es"]]]],[[52,45]],[[44,47]],[[44,48]],[[44,56]],[[44,57]],[[44,58]],[[44,59]],["H3",{"node":"[object Object]"},["DIV",{"class":"flex-shrink-0 gap-[8px] flex items-center","style":"transform: translateZ(0px);"},["IMG",{"__playwright_current_src__":"https://dev.hercules.works/icons/asterisk.svg","alt":"star icon","class":"hchat-icon flex-shrink-0","src":"/icons/asterisk.svg","style":"width: 18px; height: 18px; min-width: 18px; min-height: 18px; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; will-change: transform;"}],["DIV",{},["STRONG",{},"Key Data Points to Measure"]]]],[[44,66]],[[44,69]],[[44,70]],[[32,50]],[[32,51]],[[32,54]],[[32,55]],[[28,63]],[[28,64]],[[28,67]],[[28,68]],[[20,48]],[[20,49]],[[20,50]],[[20,51]],["H3",{"node":"[object Object]"},["DIV",{"class":"flex-shrink-0 gap-[8px] flex items-center","style":"transform: translateZ(0px);"},["IMG",{"__playwright_current_src__":"https://dev.hercules.works/icons/asterisk.svg","alt":"star icon","class":"hchat-icon flex-shrink-0","src":"/icons/asterisk.svg","style":"width: 18px; height: 18px; min-width: 18px; min-height: 18px; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; will-change: transform;"}],["DIV",{},["STRONG",{},"Expected Insights & Outcomes"]]]],[[20,58]],[[20,60]],[[20,61]],[[12,63]],[[12,64]],[[12,67]],[[12,68]],[[8,60]],[[8,61]],[[4,53]],[[4,54]],[[4,55]],[[4,56]],["H3",{"node":"[object Object]"},["DIV",{"class":"flex-shrink-0 gap-[8px] flex items-center","style":"transform: translateZ(0px);"},["IMG",{"__playwright_current_src__":"https://dev.hercules.works/icons/asterisk.svg","alt":"star icon","class":"hchat-icon flex-shrink-0","src":"/icons/asterisk.svg","style":"width: 18px; height: 18px; min-width: 18px; min-height: 18px; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; will-change: transform;"}],["DIV",{},["STRONG",{},"Methodology"]," ",["BUTTON",{"class":"text-[#027CFE] hover:text-[#005FCC] transition-colors duration-200 roboto_ffe159c6-module__GmseOq__className font-normal text-[14px] leading-[120%] underline underline-offset-[2px]"},"See why"]]]],[[4,66]],[[4,77]],[[4,78]],["P",{},"The questionnaire will use a zero-stimulus modular tracking design. The core order will be category behavior, unaided awareness, aided awareness, brand funnel, competitive benchmarking, Fortnite engagement, switching and churn, monetisation, loyalty, advocacy, and open-ended feedback. A rotating wave module may be added without changing the core KPI wording."],"\n",["P",{},"A total sample of 450 provides a practical directional baseline for overall tracking and enables comparison across major behavioral segments. Results will be interpreted using confidence intervals, significance testing, and segment base sizes rather than treating small subgroup differences as definitive. Future waves should preserve the core sample structure and field timing wherever possible."],"\n",["P",{},"The question mix will use behavioral frequency measures, fully labeled five-point scales, semantic-differential brand imagery measures, NPS, forced-choice comparisons where useful, and short open-ended probes at high-value diagnostic points. Long agree/disagree grids will be avoided to reduce acquiescence and positive-end response bias."],"\n",["P",{},["STRONG",{},"Data Collection Approach:"]," SuperJ mobile application and web"]],[[92,492]]]]]],[[92,497]],[[92,498]]]]]]]],[[276,75]],[[581,191]]]]]],[[92,521]]]]]]]]]],[[597,507]],[[597,508]],[[597,509]]],[[597,656]],[[563,151]],[[581,236]],[[563,152]],[[196,479]],[[92,531]]]],"viewport":{"width":1280,"height":720},"timestamp":368417.469,"wallTime":1786696257393,"collectionTime":3.9000000059604645,"resourceOverrides":[],"isMainFrame":true}}
